          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"hamsun-victoria-7e5e754d0a0b7199\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"Victoria directly and emphatically avows that she loves Johannes, with the reiterated focus on him reinforcing the truth-conditional content. Because this answers his request for reciprocation and is accompanied by a kiss, it weakly enacts relational acceptance, but it does not explicitly undertake a commitment. Her heaving breast, trembling, haste, and repetition show intense affect but do not independently establish expressive/reflexive force; she had deliberately deferred the declaration until reaching a more private place.\",\"ambiguity\":\"There is limited ambiguity about weak performative force: in this courtship exchange the declaration functions as an answer and relational reciprocation, but its core wording remains an avowal rather than a promise or undertaking.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Victoria directly says “Jeg elsker Dem” (“I love you”) to Johannes, then clarifies and repeats that it is he whom she loves.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Johannes has declared his love and made his hopes depend on Victoria’s answer. She postpones answering in public, questions him about Camilla, then draws him into the entranceway and gives an unambiguous reciprocal declaration, embrace, and kiss. The privacy-seeking, focused clarification, and repetition present this as a deliberate but highly emotional avowal rather than an uncontrolled verbal reflex.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jeg elsker Dem, sa hun. Forstår De det? Det er Dem jeg elsker.”\",\"supports\":\"The explicit present-tense declaration and focused clarification strongly support truth-conditional avowal.\",\"confidence\":1.0},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Johannes asks for an answer after saying, “Jeg elsker Dem og sier det nu,” and says that what follows will depend on her response.\",\"supports\":\"Victoria’s declaration functions as reciprocal acceptance within a courtship exchange, giving weak support to performative force.\",\"confidence\":0.93},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Victoria first says “Ikke her ... Jeg skal gjøre det dernede,” then later chooses the entranceway in which to declare her love.\",\"supports\":\"Her postponement and selection of the setting indicate a deliberate declaration rather than words emerging as a reflex-like discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"After speaking, she pulls him down several steps, embraces and kisses him, trembles against him, and repeats “Det er Dem jeg elsker.”\",\"supports\":\"The conduct confirms sincerity and emotional intensity, while not by itself supplying independent expressive/reflexive core force.\",\"confidence\":0.97}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the dominant avowal, with slight P support for its reciprocal relational function. The intense physical and emotional delivery is adequately represented contextually without assigning E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
